# Canvas Build Summary

## What Has Been Built

1. .canvas persistence is implemented
- Canvas state is saved as JSON with `nodes` and `edges`.
- Reopening a .canvas file restores the same layout.
- Core logic is in `src/App.tsx`, `src/components/canvas/CanvasView.tsx`, and `src/types/canvas.ts`.

2. Obsidian-style JSON canvas compatibility path exists
- .canvas files are treated as canvas documents (not markdown notes).
- The data model follows JSON-canvas style structure so imported Obsidian canvases can be opened and worked with.

3. Multiple .canvas files are supported
- One .canvas file maps to one independent layout.
- Canvas files no longer overwrite each other.
- Rename flow preserves .canvas extension behavior.

4. Canvas and graph tab workflow support
- Graph can open in tab workflow.
- Canvas opens in canvas view path instead of raw text view.
- Special tab-body rendering was added in the editor shell.

5. Canvas interaction and UX improvements
- Improved drag pointer tracking.
- Improved resize behavior to follow cursor more accurately.
- Added alignment guides/snap behavior.
- Group interaction/layering behavior improved for selection-through scenarios.

6. Canvas visual refinements
- Better control scaling at low zoom.
- Reduced zoom blur artifacts.
- Softer tab corner styling.
- Embedded note spacing and padding tuned.

7. Embedded content improvements in file nodes
- Better markdown embedding and scrolling behavior.
- Better handling of image/file previews in canvas nodes.

## Future Builds (Roadmap)

1. Replace browser prompt with in-app modal for new canvas naming
- Use the same modal UX as note creation.

2. Full JSON-canvas spec hardening
- Strict validation and round-trip support for optional fields.
- Add compatibility tests for imported Obsidian canvases.

3. Canvas tab management polish
- Add New Canvas, Duplicate Canvas, Save As, and recent canvases list.

4. Performance for large canvases
- Viewport culling/virtualization for nodes.
- Edge batching and rendering optimizations.

5. Rich editing toolset
- Multi-select transform handles.
- Align/distribute controls.
- Lock nodes and z-order commands.
- Minimap.

6. Import/export diagnostics
- Validation UI for malformed or partial canvas JSON.
- One-click repairs for common issues.

7. Autosave status and recovery
- Saved/unsaved indicator.
- Recovery snapshots for crash resilience.

